      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-02-14_WidnesExaminer_art0008" n="art0008">
        <head>CANADIAN Government LECTURE</head>
        <p>CANADIAN Government LECTURE</p>
        <p>Le eti</p>
        <p>----Laura on Canada, illustrated by Lantern Slides, will be given by °Mr. A. P' JURY. 4114(1 ian Government Emigration Agent, in the SO-OPERATIVE HALL, •-•AIRO STREET, WARRINGTON, ()I1 TUESDAY, FEB. 24, at 7-30 p.m. Doors open 7 p.m. ADMISSION FREE.</p>
        <p>c tim jiPor further particulars apply to:— A AN GOVERNMENT EMIGRATION AGENT, 48. Lord Street. Liverpool.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-02-14_WidnesExaminer_art0009" n="art0009">
        <p>ROYAL COURT THEATRE, WARRINGTON. Proprietor .............. Sir Joseph Beecham. General Manager ....... . . A. M. Loader. . Acting Manager ........... H. L. Warburton.</p>
        <p>" TIIE OLD GUARD," BY THE CROSFIELD OPERATIC SOCIETY. MONDAY, FEBRUARY Ord, For 6 nights.</p>
        <p>Prices of Admission: Boxes, 10s. 6d.; Front Stalls (Reserved), 35.; Lower Grand Circle (Reserved), Is.; Back Stalls (Reserved), 2s. 6d.; Grand Circle (Reserved), is. 6d.; Promenade, ls.; Pit, tkl. (booked day of performance, Pd.); Gallery 4d. CRI7SADE AGAINST CONSCRIPTION. A PUBLIC MEETING Will b• held in the</p>
        <p>CO-OPERATIVE HALL, CAIRO-STREET, ON THURSDAY NEXT. FEBRUARY 19th. Addresses will be given by JOHN W. BARRY, Egg• (Orgitnising Secretary of Auatralian Freedom League). " Conneription Laive of Australeaia." Rev. H. DUNNICO (formerly of Warrington). Chair to be taken at 7.45 p.m. by C. JACKSON HOLMES, Esq. Questions Invited.</p>
        <p>LYONS INTERNATIONAL 'URBAN EXIIIBITION, 1914, ON MAY it, 1914, ed the historic CITY of LYONS one of itiiehbefin orinExhibitions ever held on the Continent. It will be the apotheosis of INDUSTRY, SCIENCE AND INVENTION.</p>
        <p>The Exhibition will comprise. 90 Magnificent Palaces and Buildings, situated in the splendid Park at the junction of the Saone and the Rhone. All the nations of the earth are competing for the best positions at this forthcoming Festival of the Inventor and the Scientist, and thanks to the warm friendship uniting the hands and hearts of the French and British People</p>
        <p>THE BRITISH SECTION HAS BEEN ASSIGNED THE PLACE OF HONOUR AT THE MAIN ENTRANCE OF TEE EXHIBITION.</p>
        <p>The Magnificent Gardens will be one gigantic bouquet ot flowers, trees and ornamental shrubs. Some 12,000 gardeners are engaged in the industry of preparing Floral Masterpieces.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-02-14_WidnesExaminer_art0010" n="art0010">
        <head>POSITION.</head>
        <p>POSITION.</p>
        <p>The Exhibition is situated inside the town of Lyons. There will be a fine STADIUM and SPORTS GROUND, also a FUN CITY. As we know all nations vie in the endeavour to capture the trade, and get the largest possible share, -Irma the coffers of wealthy France.</p>
        <p>WAKE UP, ENGLAND! Germany, the United States of America, Italy and Russia, not to count the host of less important nations, are all taking important sections. Now is the time to strike, thanks to the present pecu- liarly favourable situation, to VIE ENTENTE CORDIALE. to the love and respect to which every Frenchman and French woman has for Great Britain and her people and products. All applications for space or information should be addressed to THE FRENCH CHAMBER OF COMMERCE IN LONDON, Monument-square, London, E.C.; or to the BRITISH REPRESENTATIVE, Lyons International Exhibition, London Chamber of Commerce, Oxford-court, Cannon-street, B.C. The British Representative can be seen 4t this last address every day from 9 to II a.m.</p>
      </div>
