        <p>lams generating their own. It is a common practice to scrap small generating plants if a reasonable supply of power at a reasonable rate can be obtained. Councillor Gough: Is it a fact that you are supplying a firm at halfpenny per unit? Mr. Mathias: It is not correct. Councillor Gough : Plus 71 per cent Mr. Mathias: It is the 10 per cent, for coil reasons.</p>
        <p>Mr. Hallaway : And we are not losing money on it. Councillor Gbugh : Are the Tramways Com- mittee paying three-halfpence per unit at u total' cost per year of £.3,234 18s. 4d.? Mr. Mathias: Yes. Mr. Hallaway : We have a special machine set apart for them. The Inspector: It is a low factor. Mr. Mathias: Miserable.</p>
        <p>"I had no rest with him day or night I might as wellitaveihrown away themoney I spent on common "ointments; lotions, etc., as none of them did the least good. 'A neighbour then advised Zam-Buk. So I got a box of this balm from the chemist, and Was dolightld with the relief it gave Albert. His brtrning skin teas soothed by Zam-Buk. "By dressing Albert's sores daily with Zam-Buk the inflammation died away and the mattery discharge dried up. New healthy tissue then grew. Instead of a body covered with sores there is not a mark on the boy's skin now. "Zam-Buk also cured our baby girl's severe attack of blotches.</p>
