      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-02-14_WidnesExaminer_art0070" n="art0070">
        <head>RUNCORN TRAGEDY.</head>
        <p>A RUNCORN TRAGEDY.</p>
        <p>Mrs. M. Hoffland, wife of James Hoff land, a coal merchant, residing at Norfolk-street, Run- corn, collapsed in Waterloo-road on Monday evening and died suddenly. She was middle- aged, and sometime during Monday afternoon complained to her husband of feeling unwell. Later she did not improve and went to see a doctor. After being examined and treated at the surgery, she left apparently all right. She had hardly crossed over the road, when she was seen to collapse. Pedestrians rendered aid, and Mrs. Hoff land wpis carried back into the sur- gery, where she was found to be dead. There was no inquest, as Mrs. Hoffland had been a sufferer for some time from heart trouble.</p>
      </div>
