        <p>WARHINCTON P.S.A.</p>
        <p>The Warrington P.S.A., at the Park Picture Palace on Sunday, held another of those bright, helpful services characteristic of the ideals of this movement.</p>
        <p>Mr. J. Elwell presided over a well-attended meeting and spoke on the inability Of the Churches to retain its young life. Mr. A. Mounfield gave an address on the text, St. John xxi. 25. This singular text was the subject, of a most bright, profitable and inter- esting address, which was followed with keen interest. " Mr. E. Walker gave an excellent rendering of the solo, "The Lord is light." The Excelsior Glee Party gave the two selections "Peaceful night" and• "The , long day closes." Both gave a e greatly appreciated. The ,P.S.A. Band selection, under Mr. Hannan, conductor. Miss Watts and Mr. Trow were the accompan- ists. Mr. Clegg and Mr. Wilson also took part in the meeting.</p>
