      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-02-14_WidnesExaminer_art0164" n="art0164">
        <p>Reflection Mistaken for Fire. A chimney on fire reflecting in the windows of Messrs. Garland's shop in Bridge-,street late tin Saturday night gave the impression that the shop was on fire and the brigade were called out. They discovered thp delusion. cause of the optical Pupil of Distinguished Professor. Br. W. P. (lowland, who delivered such an absorbing lecture on the "Antiquity of man" to members of the Literary and Philosophical Nociety on Monday, was a pupil and assistant 'or the late Professor Alfred Young, who fol 131411 Y years was one of the distinguished %embers of the society.</p>
        <p>Motor Cyclists Compete. 'Warrington on Saturday afternoon was the ktai, tting and finishing place of a motor cycle ,',!ce• The course extended over 75 miles and 7 race was won by the Chester Club. A lady 'TllMPetitor took part in the race. The ~.ligton War- UI) did not take part in the competi- oon.</p>
