        <p>The whales—including blue rorquals, long—are the giants of the modern won] Ed. Perrier, of the Paris Natural I</p>
        <p>Museum, points out that several species soon be lost. At least thirty companies of way are seeking whales on the African .0 and the danger from English hunters is as The Paris Academy has passed resolution! ing French and International protection.</p>
        <p>Test Oil Against Steam. Two new fuel ships, the Kanawha a' Maumee, are now under construction United States Navy. The former will lia three-cylinder triple-expansion engin 2,600 h.p. each, and is being construete private 'yard. The latter, however, will pelled by two Nurnberg Diesel engines Proximately the same power as the stel gines in the sister ship. These two ship "Power") will afford an excellent optic)] for determining the relative merits of ( steam engines under like conditions.</p>
        <p>White Rhinoceros Sought. An expedition has just gone forth to attl to secure a specimen of the white rhinoeell the wilds of the Sudanese and Abyssinia° terland. There is no white rhinoceros_...i,l; Natural History Museum in South Keil' although one has been desired for yeloB* big game hunter, led by Mr. Abel Clial3' •</p>
