        <p>By Mr. %V. BREWARD. --CLEARANCE SALE OF SURPLUS STOCK</p>
        <p>By Public iii-aron-,-fo-r-14 days only. BREWARD'S CHINA ROOMS, LYME- STREET, WARRINGTON. MR. W. BREWARD, having accumulated a large quantity of SURPLUS STOCK, will offer the same by PUBLIC AUCTION at above address each day without reserve. Sale commences SATURDAY, FEBRUARY 21st, and closes MONDAY, MARCH 9th. The quality of the goods kept by Mr. Breward is well known, and consists of the largest vavietv of Glass and China in the district, which has all been bought for his usual trade. Sale by Auction each day at 7 o'clock. Business as usual during the day. N.B.—NO SALE on THURSDAYS. By Mr; W. BOOTH.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-02-14_WidnesExaminer_art0284" n="art0284">
        <head>LAST FEW DAYS. LEAVING THE PREMISES.</head>
        <p>LAST FEW DAYS. LEAVING THE PREMISES.</p>
        <p>_ 64, and 66, SANKEY-STREET, WARRINGTON THIS DAY and following days until the Stock is - cleared.</p>
        <p>MR. W. BOOTH has -received instructions from S. Williams and Son, who are giv- ing up business in Warrington, to SELL BY AUCTION the whole of the large and high- class stock of CHINA, GLASS and ART POTTERY WARE. Sale by Auction at 3 and 7 o'clock each dati; SHOP TO LET. Fixtures will be Sold on e last day of Sale.</p>
