        <p>I '" -assessommia° ~ , Yob are ,-. „ - ....., . -N 0 T .:. ~,,,,.,,:•;!:„,•„,,,..,:::::. :,r . . . ............111.100 TOO OLD ... ::,•:.,,,:.. . .•. . ..... :• .. .•, ...• . ......_ , . ..:,, .. ..... ••• ~::::„..5...:.:.• • Read the following remarkable Letter from a Lady 68 YEARS OF AGE. Dear Mrs'. Slater,— October 13th, 1913. Two years ago I came to see you, being so ill that I bad to be led to the station, yet d and in two made a new Woman of me. I am now 68 years of age. and can do a full day's washing, or; in factanything, without feeling any ill effects, months you cure , and yet nobody could be worse than I was. I have sent you three of my friends, and you have cured them all, and I am bring- ing another to see you to-day, who is 70 years old. I only hope you will do her as much good as you have done me, but then I've never heard of 'a case that has not been a com- plete success. What this nation of poor suffering women would-do without you I don't know. I heard of you 20 years ago, but always thought my case too bad, as I'd been given up - by every. .doctor who'd seen me—they were just waiting for me to die—and still I'm here and alive—thanks to you alone. Yours faithfully, (The name and address of the writer will be given on application). • MY REMARKS. • This unsolicited testimonial must appeal to you. It is from a lady who .suffered for 20 years and had been given up by doctors and friends, and vet in two months I was able to effect a complete cure—notwithstanding her age. Better testimony than this there cannot be. This lady has already brought four of her friends to consult me. Follow her advice, and Beo me at-once—it will cost you nothing. , eONSULT ME ON WEDNESDAY NEXT. Ruptures, Women's Internal Weaknesses, Displacement, etc., , Cured and RelieVed Without Operations or Internal Implements. Our delicate organisations-render us . liable to contract internal ailments . which, if not attended to in time, may • cause us years of suffering. Mos