        <p>The first Labour Demand Circular of the Canadian Department of the Interior for Season 1914, contains particulars of no fewer than 7,650 vacancies at stated places, and Good Wages for Workers on the Land, and Domestic Servants, in the Provinces of Ontario and Quebec. All the other Provinces present 'similar opportunities. The second Labour Demand Circular con- taining details of further opportunities is already in print. CANADA ALSO OFFERS, 160 ACRES FREE. For free maps, pamphlets and full official infor- mation, apply to the Canadian Government Emigration Agent, 48, Lord Street, Liverpool: or to the Assistant Superintendent of Emigration, 11 and 12, Charin Cross, London, 8.W., or the nearest licensed Steamship Agent.</p>
